      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T10:51:47Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): floor a capped lathe C-section feed word that rounds over its cap\n\nfanuc-lathe.cps's C-axis live-tool G01 caps its composite F so the X/Z\npart stays within the machine's maximum feed and the C part within its\nstated C rate, then wrote F rounded to nearest at one decimal: a feed\nwithin half a step of its cap posted up to 0.05 mm/min over it. The\ncap is now kept as its own value and the word goes through capWord():\nunchanged unless it is over the cap, then floored to the 0.1 step at or\nunder it. Feeds away from their cap post byte-identically (no recorded\nor golden program changed).\n\nPinned by crates/post/tests/lathe_live_feed_cap.rs: a feed capped at a\nC rate between steps, a feed one step under the C cap, one under the\nlinear cap, and a feed far from (and exactly at) its cap unchanged.\n\nFixes #1392\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
