      "message": "fix(post): judge the lathe C-section feed cap on its posted words; refuse F0\n\nM3's safety review of PR #1397, and #1398:\n- liveMove measures the cap between the words the control reads (X from\n  its rounded diameter, Z origin-relative at 0.001, C at 0.001), as\n  rotaryFeed's q()/org does for the mills. A short move rounded longer\n  could drive X/Z ~7% over the maximum feed.\n- A word under the 0.1 mm/min step (a cap that floors to F0, or a tiny\n  planned feed) is refused by name, never posted as F0.\n- capWord's 1e-9 tolerance is dropped (unpinned; flooring without it is\n  only ever on the safe side).\n\nPinned by lathe_live_feed_cap: a_capped_move_is_judged_on_its_posted_words,\nan_off_lattice_stream_is_judged_on_its_posted_words,\na_cap_that_floors_under_the_f_step_is_refused_by_name,\nan_uncapped_feed_under_the_f_step_is_refused_by_name.\n\nFixes #1392\nFixes #1398\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
